Brig can store OAuth authorization codes in PostgreSQL (`oauth_auth_code` table), selected by `postgresMigration.oauthAuthCode` (`cassandra`, `migration-to-postgresql` or `postgresql`). There is no data migration: `migration-to-postgresql` behaves like `postgresql`, so codes issued before switching away from `cassandra` are lost; as codes are valid for a few minutes only, affected clients just restart the authorization flow. Expired rows are removed by the `expire-oauth-auth-code` pg_cron job when pg_cron is available.
